.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt DRIVER_ATTACH 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm driver_attach
.Nd bind a driver to a device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/driver.h
.Ft int
.Fn driver_attach "struct driver *drv" "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn driver_attach
function binds a device driver
.Fa drv
to a device
.Fa dev .
.Pp
The function performs the following steps:
.Bl -enum
.It
Verifies that the device is not already bound to a driver.
.It
Calls the
.Va attach
callback of the driver (if provided).
.It
Sets the
.Va dev->driver
pointer to
.Fa drv .
.El
.Pp
If the device is attached to a bus, the bus lock is held during the binding process to ensure atomicity.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn driver_attach
function returns 0 on success.
Otherwise, it returns -1 to indicate failure (e.g., invalid arguments, device already bound, or attach callback returned failure).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr driver_detach 9 ,
.Xr driver_register 9 ,
.Xr device_register 9
